# A short complete narrative for the parent; it refers to source-recorded categories, not newly discovered subtypes.
en=['Results candidate (final)\n','In the same 159 SLE cases and 71 references eligible for aggregate B-cell IFN analysis, the adjusted B-cell fraction differed by 0.03 percentage points (95% CI −2.26 to 2.31), whereas IFN12 differed by 0.171 (95% CI 0.130 to 0.211). The original 233-person composition estimate remains unchanged at −0.24 percentage points.','Source-recorded B states provided a more detailed comparison. Among 155 cases and 70 references with assessed state labels, naive, memory and atypical B-cell fractions differed by 8.49 (95% CI 2.90 to 14.08), −10.14 (−15.56 to −4.73) and 1.79 (0.65 to 2.93) percentage points of all B cells, respectively (BH q≤0.003). Unresolved cells remained in the denominator; five B-positive individuals with no named-state annotations were unavailable for these comparisons.','IFN12 was higher within source-recorded naive B cells (146 cases, 70 references; difference 0.165, 95% CI 0.124 to 0.206) and memory B cells (142 cases, 69 references; 0.166, 0.122 to 0.210). In the shared 136-case/69-reference population eligible for both states, the differences remained positive: 0.151 (0.111 to 0.191) and 0.169 (0.124 to 0.214). Corresponding estimates were also positive in selected processing cohort 4 and in the high-annotation-coverage analysis. These are within-source sensitivity results, not independent replication.','In the same 155-case/70-reference population, the unadjusted-for-state-mixture aggregate IFN contrast was 0.171 (0.130 to 0.212), compared with 0.134 (0.091 to 0.178) after adding the three recorded-state fractions. These estimates allow recorded composition and expression to be examined together without establishing cell-intrinsic activation. Atypical B-cell IFN was not modelled because only three references met the target-cell threshold.','Coverage note: unresolved labels accounted for 8.47% of source B cells in cases and 5.12% in references, with marked processing-cohort differences. The covariate-adjusted unresolved-fraction diagnostic did not identify a clear case–reference difference (−0.13 percentage points; 95% CI −0.95 to 0.68). This does not demonstrate equivalence or random missingness. All missing-label records, including batch-level summaries, are retained.']
zh=['结果候选段（最终）\n','在同一组159例SLE和71名参考个体中，总体B细胞比例校正差异为0.03个百分点（95%置信区间−2.26至2.31），IFN12差异为0.171（0.130至0.211）。原233人的B细胞组成估计−0.24个百分点保持不变。','来源记录的B状态提供了更细致的比较。在细标签可评估的155例病例和70名参考个体中，以全部B细胞为分母，初始、记忆及非典型B细胞比例分别相差8.49（95%置信区间2.90至14.08）、−10.14（−15.56至−4.73）和1.79（0.65至2.93）个百分点，BH q均不高于0.003。未细分细胞继续保留在分母中；5名有B细胞但三种状态标签均缺失的个体，其状态组成不可评估，不作为亚型零值。','来源初始B细胞中的IFN12差异为0.165（95%置信区间0.124至0.206；146例病例、70名参考个体），记忆B细胞中为0.166（0.122至0.210；142例病例、69名参考个体）。在两种状态均符合细胞数阈值的共同136例病例和69名参考个体中，差异仍为正，分别为0.151（0.111至0.191）和0.169（0.124至0.214）。选定处理队列4及高注释覆盖敏感性中的效应方向也一致。这些分析均来自同一来源研究，不能视作独立验证。','在同一155例病例和70名参考个体中，尚未加入状态比例时总体B细胞IFN效应为0.171（0.130至0.212）；加入三种来源状态比例后为0.134（0.091至0.178）。这有助于结合记录的细胞组成和表达结果进行解释，但不能证明细胞内在激活。非典型B细胞只有3名参考个体达到目标细胞数阈值，因此未拟合该状态内的IFN组间模型。','覆盖说明：未细分标签占病例来源B细胞的8.47%、参考个体的5.12%，不同处理队列之间也有差异。校正协变量后的未细分比例差异未达到明确证据（−0.13个百分点；95%置信区间−0.95至0.68），但这不能证明两组等价或标签随机缺失。完整缺失标签及批次汇总均予以保留。']
(W/'final_results_candidate_en.txt').write_text('\n\n'.join(en)+'\n');(W/'final_results_candidate_zh.txt').write_text('\n\n'.join(zh)+'\n')
